{"id": "EUVD-2026-102284", "enisaUuid": "211cdb1a-3f0f-3271-8e8e-5cc313e35337", "description": "SoX through 14.4.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability in lsx_ms_adpcm_block_expand_i() in src/adpcm.c, triggered by an odd samplesPerBlock value in the WAV fmt chunk. Attackers can supply a crafted MS ADPCM WAV file to sox or any libsox consumer to write a partially controlled 16-bit sample past the heap buffer allocated by wav_ms_adpcm_fmt().", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:07", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/sox-wav-ms-adpcm-samplesperblock-oob-write", "https://github.com/chirlu/sox/blob/42b3557e13e0fe01a83465b672d89faddbe65f49/src/adpcm.c#L144-L166", "https://github.com/chirlu/sox/blob/42b3557e13e0fe01a83465b672d89faddbe65f49/src/wav.c#L250-L251", "https://sourceforge.net/projects/sox/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sox-through-14.4.2-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-ms-adpcm-wav-decoding"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111157", "GHSA-c49g-67hx-w7g2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e85570bd-033e-3df1-a581-1cad96146384", "product": {"name": "SoX", "vendor": {"name": "Chris Bagwell"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226414.4.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ddc1c213-9b4b-39a5-b5b2-89d4841830d0", "vendor": {"name": "SoX"}}], "isExploited": false}